<!--
     ASUS' power profile for this tablet, from the stock framework-res: the currents in
     mA that Android multiplies by time to estimate what used the battery. Without it
     the framework falls back to AOSP's placeholder, a 1000 mAh battery where every
     consumer draws 0.1 mA.

     The numbers are stock's, unchanged. Six names are not: Nougat's keys were renamed
     by Pie, which ignores the old ones.

         cpu.idle                ->  cpu.suspend
         cpu.awake               ->  cpu.idle
         cpu.speeds.clusterN     ->  cpu.core_speeds.clusterN
         cpu.active.clusterN     ->  cpu.core_power.clusterN
         dsp.audio, dsp.video    ->  audio, video

     Pie also has cpu.active and cpu.cluster_power.clusterN, the cost of having any CPU
     or a whole cluster awake, which Nougat folded into the per-core figures; stock did
     not measure them separately, so they are left out and count as zero. The Wi-Fi keys
     are the old estimator's (wifi.on, wifi.active, wifi.scan), which Pie still uses
     when no wifi.controller.* values are given.

     The two frequency tables match the kernel's scaling_available_frequencies for the
     four Cortex-A53 (cluster 0) and the two Cortex-A72 (cluster 1).
-->
